194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 179 0 R
/T (Dear Neighbors, As we close out the first month of this new administration, I want to share an update on what we have accomplished so far and the important opportunities ahead for our city.)
/E (Dear Neighbors, As we close out the first month of this new administration, I want to share an update on what we have accomplished so far and the important opportunities ahead for our city.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 179 0 R
/T (What we have learned is encouraging. While there are real challenges to address, there are also significant opportunities. I have met with multiple corporations, businesses, and employers who are eager to invest in Vineyard. Economic interest in our city is strong, and we have real potential to expand our tax base while creating quality jobs for residents.)
/E (What we have learned is encouraging. While there are real challenges to address, there are also significant opportunities. I have met with multiple corporations, businesses, and employers who are eager to invest in Vineyard. Economic interest in our city is strong, and we have real potential to expand our tax base while creating quality jobs for residents.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 179 0 R
/T (Addressing Audit Findings and Ensuring Accountability Two independent audits completed last year identified serious concerns within certain city operations, including areas of the RDA and other functions that were flagged as very high risk. Since taking office, I have maintained regular communication with state oversight agencies as we continue to identify issues and work through the necessary reset these findings require. My commitment to you is simple and firm. We will address these matters fully, lawfully, and transparently, and we will reposition Vineyard on solid footing for the future. Transparency means more than acknowledging problems. It means investigating them thoroughly and fixing them properly. I am working with the City Council to use a portion of budget savings already achieved to fund a third, more forensic audit. This deeper review will focus specifically on the high risk areas identified previously, giving us the complete picture we need to move forward with confidence. We must understand what happened in the past to ensure it does not happen again. Restoring confidence with our state partners and with you, our residents, is essential. Self governance is a privilege that requires competence, accountability, and openness. We are committed to earning and maintaining that trust through action, not rhetoric.)
/E (Addressing Audit Findings and Ensuring Accountability Two independent audits completed last year identified serious concerns within certain city operations, including areas of the RDA and other functions that were flagged as very high risk. Since taking office, I have maintained regular communication with state oversight agencies as we continue to identify issues and work through the necessary reset these findings require. My commitment to you is simple and firm. We will address these matters fully, lawfully, and transparently, and we will reposition Vineyard on solid footing for the future. Transparency means more than acknowledging problems. It means investigating them thoroughly and fixing them properly. I am working with the City Council to use a portion of budget savings already achieved to fund a third, more forensic audit. This deeper review will focus specifically on the high risk areas identified previously, giving us the complete picture we need to move forward with confidence. We must understand what happened in the past to ensure it does not happen again. Restoring confidence with our state partners and with you, our residents, is essential. Self governance is a privilege that requires competence, accountability, and openness. We are committed to earning and maintaining that trust through action, not rhetoric.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 179 0 R
/T (Taking Stock January by the Numbers January has been focused on a comprehensive review of Vineyard City operations. I have met with staff across every department, reviewed ongoing projects, and examined staffing levels, budgets, and programs. This data gathering phase is essential. You cannot manage what you do not measure, and you cannot improve what you do not fully understand.)
/E (Taking Stock January by the Numbers January has been focused on a comprehensive review of Vineyard City operations. I have met with staff across every department, reviewed ongoing projects, and examined staffing levels, budgets, and programs. This data gathering phase is essential. You cannot manage what you do not measure, and you cannot improve what you do not fully understand.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
